Story: From plan to flight
  On: desktop
  As a pilot at the field
  I want to plan a mission, upload it and throw the plane into it
  So that it flies the mission on its own

  This tutorial shows all the steps of a flight. You plan a short circuit on the map, and
  you write it to the plane. Then you arm the plane, select AUTO and throw the plane. After
  the throw, ArduPlane flies the circuit. [[Planning a mission]] and [[Flying a mission]]
  give more information about each part.

  Scenario: Plan, upload, arm, AUTO, throw
    When the operator toggles the planning tool
    Then the map tool is PLAN
    When the operator adds a takeoff
    When the operator plans two waypoints
    When the operator adds a return home
    Then the plan has 4 items
    When the operator uploads the plan
    Then the vehicle mission is up to date
    When the operator arms the vehicle
    Then the vehicle is armed
    When the operator switches to AUTO
    Then the autopilot mode is AUTO
    When the pilot throws the plane in the sim
    Then the plane is flying the mission
